<%# locals: (teams:)

    The pick board, phone-sized: six recognizable teams from
    TurfMonsterRules::SHOWCASE (real ranks and opponents, board order), drawn
    with the SAME static card the v1 rules page
    uses (pages/_rules_team_card), which reads every colour from
    TeamColorsHelper#team_card_palette. Nil-safe end to end: a missing Team row
    draws a neutral card with the slug's name, never a 500.

    DRAWN AT BOARD SIZE, THEN SHRUNK. The compact card at a phone's half-width
    crams its three opponent columns into ~30px each, which drops the team
    names (and at the lg breakpoint the chips step up to text-sm). So the
    screen is laid out wider than the frame and scaled to 0.66 from the
    top-left corner (1 / 0.66 = 1.515): the cards keep the proportions they
    have on a real phone, and the frame clips whatever falls off the bottom. %>
<div class="w-[151.5%] origin-top-left scale-[0.66] px-3 pb-3" data-test="phone-pick-board">
  <%# The app bar as the real mobile navbar draws it (layouts/_navbar): the
      mascot from the same /icon-192.png at the collapsed mobile size (2.5rem),
      beside the wordmark at its collapsed mobile size (1.25rem). %>
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-1 pt-1 pb-2">
    <p class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xl font-extrabold text-heading">
      <img src="/icon-192.png" alt="" width="40" height="40" class="h-10 w-10 rounded-full shadow-lg" data-test="phone-nav-logo">
      <span>Turf <span class="tm-wordmark">Monster</span></span>
    </p>
    <p class="text-[10px] font-semibold text-muted"><%= TurfMonsterRules::SHOWCASE.size %> of 6 picked</p>
  </div>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-2">
    <% TurfMonsterRules::SHOWCASE.each do |example| %>
      <%= render "pages/rules_team_card", example: example, teams: teams, compact: true, board_style: true %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-3 rounded-full bg-primary py-2.5 text-center text-xs font-bold text-white shadow-lg shadow-primary/30">
    Hold to confirm
  </div>
</div>
